## afmail Workspace Rules

For afmail operations, follow the installed `agent-first-mail` skill. If the
skill is missing, run `afmail skill install --agent codex --scope workspace` from
this directory and restart the agent so it reloads skills.

Known afmail workspaces from this directory:
{% for workspace in workspaces %}
- `{{ workspace }}`
{% endfor %}

When operating on a listed workspace, run afmail commands with the command
working directory set to that workspace path. Do not manually edit `.afmail/`;
it is machine-managed state. Customize generated Markdown templates under
`templates/` inside the workspace.

Use `afmail` for message disposition, case membership, archive changes, push
queue changes, and remote effects.

Match agent-authored reasons, case/archive names, summaries, notes, and draft
bodies to `.afmail/config.json` `workspace.language_bcp47` unless the user asks
for another language. Put mailbox-specific exceptions outside this managed block.
